<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ihosy</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ihosy is a town in south-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, the capital of the Ihorombe region, on the main road between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fianarantsoa">Fianarantsoa</a> and Toliara. It lies on the grassy plateau of the Bara people, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> herders whose ruling Zafimanely houses established their authority over the region's clans by the 17th century. The town is a market for the zebu cattle trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ihosy.jpg" alt="Ihosy" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jose Antonio · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ihosy.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
